course: dictionary
lesson: 6996
title: Paradise and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the clues around it show you which one to use. Paradise is a good example. Its first meaning is a perfect, happy place, like a beautiful garden. «A shopper's paradise» means a place where a shopper feels perfectly happy.
explain: Its second meaning is heaven. In many religions, paradise is the perfect place that good people go to after life. «Muslims believe that after death the soul waits until the Day of Judgement; the good go to Paradise, called Jannah.» The words about judgement and after death tell you this is a religious meaning, not a garden.
explain: Its third meaning is a name. Paradise can be part of the name of a bird, a shop or a place, so it often starts with a capital letter. «Paradise tree snakes» are a kind of snake, and paradise is part of its name. Always check the clues, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Paradise means a perfect, happy place, like a beautiful garden.
fact: In many religions, paradise means heaven, a perfect place after life.
fact: «Jannah» is the name Muslims use for Paradise.
fact: «Birds of paradise» have bright feathers, and paradise is part of their name.
fact: «Paradise tree snakes» flatten their bodies and wriggle in the air to glide from tree to tree.
exercise: «The sweet shop was a paradise for kids.» What does paradise mean here? | *A perfect, happy place | A school for young children | A shop that sells sand | A dark, cold cave
exercise: «The good go to Paradise, called Jannah.» In this sentence, what does paradise mean? | A shop that sells gifts | *Heaven, a perfect place after life | A big hill with a view | A kind of snake
exercise: Find the word that tells you paradise is part of a name: «Paradise tree snakes flatten their bodies and wriggle in the air.» | Bodies | Air | *Tree | Flatten
test: «Birds of paradise have bright feathers.» What kind of word is paradise in this sentence? | A word for a loud noise | *Part of the name of a kind of bird | A word for a shop door | A word for a tree
test: Ellie says «others rebirth, judgement and Paradise» about what happens after death. What does Paradise mean in her sentence? | A name for a school | A kind of food | A village in Borneo | *One belief about what happens after death
exam: Which sentence uses paradise to mean a perfect, happy place? | *«The island was a paradise of warm sun and clear blue sea.» | «Paradise tree snakes glide between trees.» | «Muslims believe the good go to Paradise.»
